  "name": "Wander",
  "tagline": "Bloom · six loops of brighter tones, wider range, the colour rising toward Lydian.",
  "description": "Six loops of soft mallet and felt tones over a major-seventh chord, quicker and wider-ranging than Garden. The colour wanders between Mixolydian, Ionian and Lydian, one note at a time, and the palette sometimes opens from the pentatonic to the whole mode. A large room and a ping-pong echo.",
  "use": {
    "name": "Ideate",
    "for": "Generating options: brainstorming, sketching directions, combining ideas loosely.",
    "why": "The only positive evidence for sound in ideation is for livelier, brighter music on divergent thinking (happy music raised divergent scores, d = .55, sub-scores did not survive correction: weak), and moderate ambient sound may help (one study, contested). Wander is the brightest, most varied place in Field: more loops, more wandering between notes, bright modes. It is not for converging on one hard problem: music of every kind cut insight solutions against quiet (rule 37). Evidence: weak; the Lab decides."
  },
